From 13178309cdba9ef3671f5e562d37995ec8d7921e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:43:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure flat-file open and seek failures

Preserve Info, original unquoted path text, fopen/fseek/fclose ordering and
null returns. Use a distinct unsigned FileOffset key for the byte position,
not Bytes or FileNumber. Do not add errno reads or FILE pointer fields.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0, reviewed exact calls/registry addition):
  /private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/flatfile-open-diagnostics.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/flatfile227-apply.json --apply
  git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/flatfile.cpp src/test/logging_event_tests.cpp

Manual tests call actual FlatFileSeq::Open for a nonexistent read-only file
(and verify its directory was not created), and a POSIX FIFO held open on
both ends in the same test process so read-only fopen cannot wait. No bytes
are exchanged; real fseek fails with ESPIPE. Tests inspect null returns,
exact text, raw path, level and typed offset after Flush. No production API
visibility is changed. POSIX FIFO case is not compiled on Windows.

A read-only libc microprobe showed macOS /dev/urandom fseek succeeds, so
that assumed failure fixture was rejected before any native test. Use a
real unseekable owned FIFO instead; the probe receipt is retained.

Validation at commit: event lint435 sites and whitespace pass. Actual
native/FIFO gates pending with the coherent seven-field registry batch;
immutable native215 proof remains unchanged. Tier: shared eCash.
